  "description": "ADO.NET data provider for Visual FoxPro / dBase tables and database containers, built on CrossVault.FoxDbf. Use FoxPro/dBase data from Dapper, raw ADO.NET, reporting, and LINQPad via SQL: FoxDbfConnection / FoxDbfCommand / FoxDbfDataReader / FoxDbfParameter / FoxDbfConnectionStringBuilder / FoxDbfProviderFactory. Connection string mirrors the VFP OLE DB Provider (Data Source = .dbc | directory | .dbf; Collate; Exclusive; Deleted; Ansi; ReadOnly; Accelerator=Highlike). Supports SELECT (INNER/LEFT/RIGHT/FULL JOIN, UNION, correlated subqueries, GROUP BY, aggregates, ORDER BY, TOP), INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE, CREATE/ALTER/DROP TABLE, the VFP work-area model (USE/SELECT), positional ? and named @/: parameters, real transactions (atomic rollback), DataAdapter/CommandBuilder, GetSchema metadata, and a static DBF-header type map. Output is byte-compatible with the real Visual FoxPro 9 runtime.",
